# OpenMC generated inputs/outputs
*.xml
*.h5
*.out
run_results/

# Generated plots. ALL of them, including plots/ — there is no exception.
#
# There used to be a `!plots/*.png` re-inclusion for "curated verification
# plots". That exception was the defect: it made generated artifacts
# publishable, and twelve plots depicting geometry that no longer existed
# (60 cm plates, 15 cm end-box, 8x9 lattice, 2.5 cm flux trap) sat tracked in
# the repository from 2026-07-27 until the Phase 1 audit found them.
#
# Generators are tracked and are deterministic — tests/plot_core.py and
# tests/make_phase1_xs_plots.py both rebuild their output from geometry.py
# constants alone. Tracking the generator is sufficient; tracking its output
# means the repository can assert something the code does not.
*.png

# figures/ tracks SOURCE ONLY (make_figures.py, check_figures.py, figstyle.py).
# Everything it emits is regenerable from those three plus geometry.py, and the
# PDFs run to several MB apiece.
*.pdf
figures/_proof/
figures/solidworks_*.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
